| The forge sync reads (#6349, epic #6348): `forge/changes`, `forge/ids`, `forge/checks` and `forge/sources` on the host, for a client cache that keeps its own changed-since cursor. `forge/changes` reads a source's issues and pull requests updated at or after a time, in every state: GitHub by search with `updated:>=`, in windows of `updated:<=` past search's 1,000 results, after a REST probe of the repo's newest item with its ETag kept (a 304 costs no rate limit, and the last answer is given again); GitLab by `updated_after`, one list per project for every state; Jira by `updated >= "-Nm"`; Linear by an `updatedAt` filter; the others by their lists, newest first, cut at the time. `forge/ids` is the ids of a source's items now, 1,000 a page; `forge/checks` is up to 100 pull requests' checks in one GraphQL call on GitHub (from the list of open pull requests elsewhere); `forge/sources` is the machine's sources, with no forge call. Each call logs its forge calls and their times | Mac, web (no client reads them yet: #6352) | tested with fakes | 2026-11-19, `Go/internal/agentsd/forgesync_test.go` (since, pages past the search limit, the probe, a failed source, ids, checks, sources), `Go/internal/githubmcp/sync_test.go` (a 304 with the ETag, many checks in one call), and the filter tests of `gitlabmcp`, `jiramcp` and `linearmcp` | `Go/internal/agentsd/forgesync.go`, `Go/internal/githubmcp/sync.go` | not yet read on a real account; Jira's relative time is of the Jira server's clock; the probe is GitHub's only |
